From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: j7prime p2 <p2@j7prime.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:53:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] dt-bindings: clock: samsung,exynos7870-cmu: add
 CMU_CPUCL0 and CMU_CPUCL1

Document the two CPU cluster clock controllers of the Exynos7870
(CMU_CPUCL1 at 0x10800000, CMU_CPUCL0 at 0x10900000). Each takes the
26 MHz OSCCLK and the cluster switch clock from CMU_MIF, the alternate
parent the CPU clock parks on while the cluster PLL relocks.

The clock IDs are added to the header together with the driver in the
next patch (as in the original series).

Origin: j7prime p2 series (new for 7.3.4), describing the nodes of
Alessandro Fontana's commit b896c79c2d22 ("clk: samsung: exynos7870:
model CMU_CPUCL0 and CMU_CPUCL1").
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---

Notes:
    Origin: new in the j7prime p2 series for v7.3.4 (see the Origin line in the message).

 .../clock/samsung,exynos7870-cmu.yaml         | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos7870-cmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos7870-cmu.yaml
index 3c58712..2923f3f 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos7870-cmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos7870-cmu.yaml
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     enum:
       - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-mif
+      - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-cpucl0
+      - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-cpucl1
       - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-dispaud
       - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-fsys
       - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-g3d
@@ -69,6 +71,25 @@ allOf:
           items:
             - const: oscclk
 
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          contains:
+            enum:
+              - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-cpucl0
+              - samsung,exynos7870-cmu-cpucl1
+    then:
+      properties:
+        clocks:
+          items:
+            - description: External reference clock (26 MHz)
+            - description: CPU cluster switch clock (from CMU_MIF)
+
+        clock-names:
